The guessed-limits warning now fires for google. gemini-2.5-pro, gemini-2.5-flash, gemini-2.5-flash-lite and gemini-2.0-flash each print the standard warning on stderr, giving the limits they actually run on: a 1M window and max_tokens = 8192. Build, all tests, clippy with -D warnings and the fmt check all pass. Committed as b57d1e07, "Part of #1021".

What changed
• How a guessing id is detected. The old check was a hand list of providers matched against == 128K && == 4096. Now an id counts as guessing when it gets the same limits as two made-up ids (zz-unknown-a, zz-unknown-b), those two agree, and no real preset covers it. "Real preset" means declared_output_ceiling (the anthropic and openai presets, plus deepseek's single preset for the whole provider) or vendor_preset. The hand list OPENAI_BASE_FALLBACK_PROVIDERS is gone.
• The google path never called the warning at all, which the plan didn't mention. So changing the check alone wouldn't have been enough. I added one helper, warn_once_if_guessing, and call it from both the google and OpenAI-compatible branches of build_agent. That made agent_builder.rs 7 lines shorter.

Tests (in src/model_limits_note.rs)
• The four gemini ids each warn, checked against the full exact text with assert_eq!.
• Still silent: gemini-3.8-flash, gemini-4-argon, the anthropic default, deepseek, ollama and custom.
• The text for an unknown openai id is unchanged byte for byte.
• A check that the two made-up ids really get the same limits on every provider, so the new check can't pass by accident.
• A list of which providers' unknown ids warn, checked by name.
• Positive control: I put the old hand list back inside the check, with a NEUTERED marker. Exactly the four tests that depend on the new check failed by name. I then restored it, the tests passed again and no marker was left.

Rows that moved in the register test, which I updated rather than deleted:
• minimax's default, MiniMax-M2.7, now warns. It runs on 1M / 4096, and it is the case the Day-224 lesson said the old check was leaving out.
• bedrock's default now counts as guessing (200K / 16000) but no warning is printed for it (see below).

Not covered by this change, and noted on #1021:
• The anthropic and bedrock branches still don't call the warning. Anthropic ids without a preset and every bedrock id run on a 200K / 16000 guess, and nobody tells the user.
• Giving the four gemini-2.x ids real limits, or deciding whether they belong on the known list at all.

I also corrected docs/src/configuration/models.md, which said minimax isn't warned about and listed only the OpenAI-compatible providers. I added an ARCHITECTURE.md entry for src/model_limits_note.rs, which didn't have one. I posted on #1021 naming the commit and quoting the 01:30:35Z note it carries out.
